// src/v2/std/value_carrier.dag
// Scope: declared structural-persistence and sharing facts for the runtime
//   collection carriers (ctrl#1533 M-A) and name-interning facts (M-D),
//   placed at the v2.std authority per the ctrl#1534 placement amendment
//   (§3–4). The v2 host interpreter
//   IMPLEMENTS these facts (ctrl#1533 phase 2); emitted Rust implements the
//   same facts by ownership analysis (move + copy-on-write). Neither layer is
//   the authority; this module is.
// Status: model-first. Phase-0 receipts (gunbc PR #4653): v2 workloads make
//   zero native mutation-primitive calls — v2 collections are closure-chain
//   maps and FreeMonoid trees, so the host copy cost rides the
//   free_monoid_to_vec flatten chokepoint. The carrier facts below are the
//   "unified runtime representation" the B-LIST-FREEMONOID-1 and
//   B-MAP-LOOKUP-OPTION-C-1 interims (v2.std.collection) dissolve against.
// Anchors: Driscoll–Sarnak–Sleator–Tarjan, "Making Data Structures
//   Persistent" (JCSS 1989); Okasaki, "Purely Functional Data Structures"
//   (1998); Bagwell, "Ideal Hash Trees" (2001); Bagwell & Rompf, "RRB-Trees"
//   (2011). Production consensus: Clojure/Scala collections; Rust im/rpds.

module v2.std.value_carrier

import v2.std.node { Symbol }

// Structural persistence of a value carrier under update: a Persistent
// carrier leaves every prior version valid (the new version structurally
// shares unchanged substructure with its predecessor); an Ephemeral carrier
// invalidates the prior version, so an immutable-value host must copy it in
// full before updating — the quadratic-allocation term ctrl#1533 measured.
// Distinct concept from product.compute_fabric.PersistenceKind (storage
// durability across restarts): same word, different DAG-ancestor — this one
// hangs off value-update semantics, not infrastructure lifecycle.
// 🟢 terminal — Practice 4 (docs/modeling-discipline.md §4) — the distinction
// is grounded in external authority (Driscoll–Sarnak–Sleator–Tarjan 1989's
// definition of a persistent structure), not an interim of ours. Step-2: the
// arms are mutually exclusive properties of one carrier under update, not
// coordinates over another axis. Patterns 1–5 N/A: no payloads to unify, no
// richer named source; the carrier itself is an external structure referenced
// by Symbol, so there is nothing here to dissolve into.
type PersistenceKind = Ephemeral | Persistent

// Symbolic work bounds in the std.primitives PrimitiveContract `work`
// convention (n = collection size). Declared per carrier so per-primitive
// cost facts (ctrl#1533 M-B) derive from the carrier instead of floating.
type CarrierCost {
  update_work: String
  lookup_work: String
}

// A carrier declaration binds an abstract collection to the host structure
// implementing it, its persistence kind, and the cost facts that persistence
// kind grounds. The interpreter and emitted code are both implementations of
// these declarations; disagreement about update cost resolves by reading the
// data values below, not by reading host source.
type CarrierDeclaration {
  collection: Symbol
  carrier: Symbol
  persistence: PersistenceKind
  cost: CarrierCost
}

// Map<K,V> carrier: hash array mapped trie (Bagwell 2001), persistent per
// Driscoll–Sarnak–Sleator–Tarjan 1989.
data map_carrier: CarrierDeclaration = {
  collection: ^map_collection,
  carrier: ^hash_array_mapped_trie,
  persistence: Persistent,
  cost: { update_work: "log32 n", lookup_work: "log32 n" }
}

// List<T> carrier: relaxed radix balanced tree (Bagwell & Rompf 2011) or a
// catenable structure consistent with FreeMonoid<T> (Okasaki 1998) — the
// carrier must realize the FreeMonoid algebra without per-site flattening
// (the free_monoid_to_vec chokepoint the phase-0 receipts identified as the
// actual copy path on v2 workloads).
data list_carrier: CarrierDeclaration = {
  collection: ^list_collection,
  carrier: ^relaxed_radix_balanced_tree,
  persistence: Persistent,
  cost: { update_work: "log n", lookup_work: "log n" }
}

// The sharing law: structural sharing between values is UNOBSERVABLE at the
// language level. A value denotes its structure alone; whether two
// structurally equal values occupy one allocation or two changes cost, never
// meaning. This law is what makes a carrier swap behavior-preserving by
// construction, and it is the claim the ctrl#1533 phase-2 verification must
// keep green. Host values are thread-confined (Rc-discipline): sharing never
// introduces concurrent observation, so the law has no hidden
// synchronization premise.
//
// The law is declared as EXECUTABLE WITNESSES, not a data type
// (v2.test.std_grounding.value_carrier_laws): a sharing-receipt type
// would have no constructor until the phase-2 swap lands, and dead vocabulary
// is the Practice-4 failure mode. If phase 2 needs a receipt, it lands with
// its first producer.

// ── Name interning (ctrl#1533 M-D) ─────────────────────────────────────────
// A runtime value's type name, variant name, and record field keys are drawn
// from CLOSED, compile-time-known sets — the declared types of the resolved
// graph (M4: closed sets are enums, not strings). The fact: those names are
// REFERENCES into the graph's declared name set, not free strings.
// v2.std.runtime already encodes this structurally (RuntimeFieldValue.field
// is a Symbol; aggregate_type is a Node); the v2 host's owned-String
// type_name and string-keyed field maps are an implementation gap, licensed
// to close in phase 3 (intern names; store record fields positionally
// against the type's declared field order). The positional-record layout —
// the largest per-instance saving the phase-0 receipts identified (12.7 MB
// of Record sharing hits, 31.8K un-interned Strings) — DERIVES from this
// fact; it is not a hand-rolled optimization.

// 🟢 terminal — Practice 4 (docs/modeling-discipline.md §4) — the three name
// domains of a value representation are a closed set fixed by the value
// model itself (a value names its type, its variant, and its fields —
// nothing else); M4 grounds enum-not-string. Patterns 1–5 N/A: no payloads
// to unify, no richer named source.
type NameDomain = TypeNames | VariantNames | FieldNames

// One declaration per name domain: where its closed set is declared
// (authority) and the host representation duty interning licenses.
type NameInterningDeclaration {
  domain: NameDomain
  authority: Symbol
  representation: Symbol
}

data type_name_interning: NameInterningDeclaration = {
  domain: TypeNames,
  authority: ^resolved_graph_declared_types,
  representation: ^interned_symbol_id
}

data variant_name_interning: NameInterningDeclaration = {
  domain: VariantNames,
  authority: ^resolved_graph_declared_variants,
  representation: ^interned_symbol_id
}

data field_name_interning: NameInterningDeclaration = {
  domain: FieldNames,
  authority: ^resolved_graph_declared_fields,
  representation: ^positional_slot_in_declared_field_order
}
